1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,677
Waterstone Financial's third quarter:
a stronger bank, a weaker mortgage
business.

2
00:00:06,227 --> 00:00:09,518
Earnings fell twenty percent to
thirty-six cents a share.

3
00:00:10,068 --> 00:00:16,670
The margin rose thirty basis points to
three point oh six percent, still the
lowest of four Wisconsin banks.

4
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:21,275
The mortgage arm lost about half a
million dollars as rates jumped.

5
00:00:21,825 --> 00:00:25,988
And nonperforming assets doubled,
mostly on one loan relationship.

6
00:00:26,538 --> 00:00:31,869
Higher interest income could not
offset three million dollars less in
mortgage-driven fees.

7
00:00:32,419 --> 00:00:38,444
In the chief executive's words,
mortgage volume was hindered by a
significant jump in mortgage rates.

